  "testId": "testim-migrated/tests/webstore/checkout/validate-checkout-page-functionalities-for-retail-user.spec.ts > Webstore - Checkout > validate checkout page functionalities for retail user",
  "scenario": {
    "summary": "A registered retail user signs in, empties the cart, adds a simple product (qty 5), checks out, edits the first saved address to a Canada address, picks the Canada shipping method, checks the order-summary line and labels, checks the payment methods and that Purchase Order and COD selection is exclusive, then empties the cart and logs out. No order is placed.",
    "steps": [
      "Sign in with the dedicated retail account (username/password from the test data); 'Hello,' greeting.",
      "Empty the cart; search the simple product SKU, open it, read the unit price, set quantity 5, add to cart, open the cart and proceed to checkout.",
      "Edit the first address card: Display Name, names, phone, street, country, state, postal code, city; save; select CanadaShipping2 (or CanadaShipping).",
      "Check the line: quantity, unit x qty = line total, Qty./Total labels, Remove link if present, Shipping label.",
      "Check the PurchaseOrder label text and the PurchaseOrder/InvoiceMe/COD labels; radios unchecked; select Purchase Order, then COD (Purchase Order unchecked).",
      "Empty the cart, check the empty-cart message, log out and check the Sign In heading."
    ],
    "entitiesTouched": [
      "user",
      "product",
      "address",
      "shipping",
      "payment",
      "cart"
    ],
    "stateChanges": [
      "The user's first saved address is overwritten with the test's Canada address",
      "Registered user's cart emptied, filled with the simple product, then emptied again",
      "No order is placed"
    ],
    "assertions": [
      "lblUserName contains 'Hello,'",
      "Line quantity equals productQuantity (5); unit price > 0 and |unit x qty - line total| <= 0.05",
      "Qty. / Total / Shipping labels",
      "paymentLabel(PurchaseOrder) text equals 'PurchaseOrder'; PurchaseOrder, InvoiceMe, COD labels visible",
      "Radios unchecked; Purchase Order checked after click; COD checked and Purchase Order unchecked after clicking COD",
      "Empty cart message visible; Sign In heading after logout"
    ],
    "evidence": [
      "Title 'validate checkout page functionalities for retail user' and the step labels match the flow.",
      "Credentials (masked) name the existing registered user: USER_WEBSTORE_REGISTERED with preferred.required true (credential source).",
      "simpleProduct z-1002656 and productId 933: tda rows shows PimProductId 933, active SimpleProduct; PRODUCT_SIMPLE_IN_STOCK quantityUsed 5, outputs sku and productId.",
      "Profile (atstage 2026-10-31) has no observations for the checkout specs: every source is profiled false. Values were checked read-only with `tda rows` where noted.",
      "Store MaxwellsHardware: the store every migrated webstore spec runs on (as in the approved shopping-cart and PDP entries); not named in the scan.",
      "selectCOD/codRadio pays with COD (txtCOD): PAYMENT_COD_ON_STORE. No source carries the COD code the page object uses, so the need has no data source.",
      "The address values (masked) overwrite the user's first saved address: created-by-test; recorded under stateChanges. DOUBT: the test needs the account to have at least one saved address (editAddressButton.first()); USER_WEBSTORE_REGISTERED does not constrain that.",
      "MISSING KEY: the CanadaShipping2 / CanadaShipping custom shipping method on the store for a CA destination; tda rows shows both (ShippingId 9 and 10, Custom, CA) have no shipping rule, so SHIPPING_FLAT_RATE_ON_STORE does not cover them. Need left out.",
      "MISSING KEY: Purchase Order and Invoice Me payment methods offered on the store to the registered user's profile. Needs left out; purchaseOrderText is asserted as label text (expected-output) and the paymentMethods codes are config.",
      "swap: data only through loadData (simpleProduct -> product.sku, productId -> product.productId; credentials kept), no derived assertions (unit price read from the page; labels fixed UI text), no data value in the spec code (z-1002656 and spnRetailPrice933 appear only in comments), no other data file."
    ],
    "confidence": "low",
    "needsReview": true
  },
